  "final_text": "cobalt_app is deployed, and the tests found no failures. But the checks that need a signed-in user didn't run, so the tests aren't finished yet.\n\n**What's done**\n- **Deploy:** finished. The app is live at https://cobalt-ledger.rehearsal.invalid.\n- **Tests:** none of the five test groups failed. In three of them (functional, accessibility and responsiveness), the checks that need a signed-in user were skipped, so those parts haven't been tested.\n\n**What I need from you**\n\nTo run those checks, the tests have to sign in as a real user. The app signs people in with a one-time code sent by email, so I need a code from someone who can sign in to cobalt_app. Sending that email counts as contacting someone, so I need your yes first.\n\n1. Reply with the email address that can sign in to cobalt_app, and say I may send it a code.\n2. A six-digit code will arrive at that address within about a minute. It works for ten minutes.\n3. Paste just the six digits here.\n\nThis is safe to paste in chat, unlike the Resend key. The code works once and expires in ten minutes. The sign-in it gets is kept in a private file on this machine and never shown. Once I have it, I'll re-run the skipped checks and tell you the results.",
